       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in PAN:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " mild to moderate dz (no serious neuro, renal, GI or cardiac manifestations): corticosteroids + MTX (or azathioprine) may be used."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " preg (non-neoplastic dz); Hx of severe hypersensitivity incl. anaphylaxis. Verify preg status b4 starting."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " embryo-fetal toxicity, hypersensitivity, severe SE, med errors. Serious SE incl. death (bone marrow, GI, liver, lungs, skin, kidneys). Myelosuppression can be severe (pancytopenia). Hepatotoxicity (fibrosis, cirrhosis), higher risk w heavy EToH use. Pulm toxicity: acute or chronic interstitial pneumonitis, can be irreversible or fatal. Severe skin rxns (SJS/TEN). Renal toxicity."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Blood counts, liver tests and renal funct @ baseline and periodically."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "↑ MTX levels/toxicity w:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ASA & other NSAIDs; penicillins & sulfonamides (incl. other antifolates); PPIs; probenecid. ⍉nitrous oxide anesthesia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Take once wkly as a single dose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " taking the wkly dose daily has caused fatal toxicity. ⍉excess sun; use sun protection. Live vaccines ⍉recommended. Do ⍉breastfeed."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
